Subject: [PATCH] Fix Agon VDP display glitches, phantom keystrokes, and Break polling

1. driver-DODVR.S:
   - Replaces DI with NOP in DO_RET1, zVDCTL3, and z_VDCTL so interrupts remain
     enabled during character display and cursor operations. On Agon Light 2,
     video memory is pumped across UART0 by the 60 Hz timer interrupt; leaving
     interrupts disabled causes tight program loops (e.g. BASIC RUN) to starve
     timer interrupts, preventing screen refresh and locking up the system.

2. driver-UART0.S:
   - Removes UART0_MSR CTS polling in CANISND (replacing with NOPs). Agon Light 2
     does not connect hardware CTS on UART0, and in the emulator CTS deasserts
     when buffers are full, freezing transmission.
   - Add VDP binary packet decoder: filters out VDP metadata packets (0x86
     PACKET_MODE, 0x89 PACKET_MOUSE, etc.) to prevent packet payloads from
     being misinterpreted as ASCII keystrokes (e.g. 0x50 'P').
   - Handles 0x81 PACKET_KEYCODE dynamically for 2-byte or 4-byte payloads:
     decodes ASCII keystrokes, Ctrl-C, Escape, and Pause without stalling on
     shorter payloads.
   - Maps both Escape (0x1B) and Ctrl-C (0x03) to Break (setting KFLAG$ bit 0
     and returning 80h in CLBUF), removing esccount countdown and hard zABORT
     task exit to prevent abrupt termination back to DOS.
   - Adds timeout loop in u0_gb to prevent infinite busy-wait in interrupt handlers.
   - Adds one-time startup FIFO drain on first CKINP call to discard stale
     packets queued by Quark MOS, loadfont, and OSboot.
   - Calls hide_vdp_cursor on first CKINP call using TXUART0 flow control to send
     VT100 ESC [ ? 25 l and Agon VDU cursor suppression sequences to eliminate the
     persistent blinking block cursor.
   - Changes CTLUART0 relative jumps to absolute jumps to avoid branch range errors.

3. ipl-strings.s:
   - Updates vt100_clear$ to include ESC [ ? 25 l and CLS (12).
   - Updates vt100_home$ to include ESC [ f and VDU 30.

4. ipl_sessions.s & ipl-trsdos.s:
   - Ensures realtim session initializes session_cmd$ with spaces instead of
     "cls", allowing clean IPL exit via SYS_EXIT 0 to the command prompt.
   - Sets initial cursor location to row 0, col 0.

5. interrupt_handler.s:
   - Fixes video buffer pump length from CRTSIZE+2 to CRTSIZE+9 so all 1920
     video RAM bytes are refreshed across UART0 along with the 9-byte prefix.
   - Removes UART0_MSR CTS polling in canisend1 (replacing with NOPs) to prevent
     infinite wait on unrouted CTS in the 60 Hz timer interrupt handler.

6. scan-kflag.s:
   - Replaces legacy TRS-80 memory-mapped keyboard matrix scanning (0xF440, KB7)
     with UART0 polling via CKINP, allowing TSTBRK during the 60 Hz timer
     interrupt to detect Break / Ctrl-C (0x03) and Break without consuming/clearing
     KFLAG$ bit 0 so that BASIC's @CKBRKC can trap the Break and return to the
     Ready prompt without exiting to DOS.

